<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 11 and older (fullBackupContent). The Android 12+ rules are in
  spool_data_extraction_rules.xml and must be kept saying the same thing.

  Auto Backup is on — the Expo template sets android:allowBackup="true" — and it
  excludes only cache/, code_cache/ and no_backup/ by default. Everything else
  under the data directory goes to Google's servers and comes back on any device
  the user restores to.

  For most of this app that is a feature: the library index in databases/ is
  worth carrying to a new phone. For two directories it is not.

  * app_webview/ is where the WebView keeps its cookie jar, which after a sign-in
    holds the user's live YouTube session. Backing that up uploads the login and
    restores it onto another device — a copy of the credential leaving the phone
    entirely, with no one deciding it should. Excluded outright.

  * spool_trial.xml is the trial's save counter. A backup taken at zero saves and
    restored later would set it back to zero, so leaving it in makes the cloud a
    reset button. (The externalMediaDirs mirror would still catch it, since it is
    outside the data directory and survives more than this does — but the two
    should not disagree in the first place.)
-->
<full-backup-content>
  <exclude domain="root" path="app_webview" />
  <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="spool_trial.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
